.TH V3DTOP 1 "October 2026" "v3dtop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
v3dtop \- btop-style live monitor for the Raspberry Pi V3D GPU
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo v3dtop
.RI [ -i\ seconds ]
.RI [ --once ]
.RI [ --json ]
.RI [ --no-trace ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B v3dtop
is a zero-dependency terminal monitor for the open-source
.B v3d
driver on the Raspberry Pi. It shows real per-engine GPU utilisation computed
from the
.B drm-engine-*
nanosecond counters in DRM
.IR fdinfo ,
clock/thermal/throttle state from
.BR vcgencmd
and debugfs, the static capability sheet from
.IR v3d_ident ,
and live job-submit rates from the
.B v3d
and
.B gpu_scheduler
ftrace tracepoints.
.PP
Root is required to read other processes' fdinfo engine counters and to use the
tracepoint panel. The tracepoint counters are collected through a private ftrace
instance under
.I /sys/kernel/tracing/instances/v3dtop
which is removed on exit, so the global trace buffer is never disturbed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -i " seconds"
Refresh interval (default 0.5).
.TP
.B --once
Render a single frame and exit.
.TP
.B --json
Emit one machine-readable JSON sample and exit.
.TP
.B --no-trace
Skip the tracepoint submit panel.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print usage and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.TP
.B p
Pause / resume the display.
.TP
.B t
Toggle the Job-submits (tracepoint) panel.
.TP
.BR + " / " -
Refresh faster / slower, in 0.1 s steps.
.SH ENGINES
RENDER (fragment/pixel work), BIN (geometry binning), CSD (compute dispatch),
TFU (texture formatting), CPU (CPU-side jobs), CACHE (cache cleans). Each is shown
as busy-time divided by wall-time for the interval.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on normal exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/*/fdinfo/*
Per-client DRM engine and memory counters.
.TP
.I /sys/kernel/debug/dri/0/
v3d_ident and measure_clock.
.TP
.I /sys/kernel/tracing/instances/v3dtop/
Private ftrace instance (created and removed by v3dtop).
